411 false] [17592186058960 1080 "$\\$3.43$ per gallon" 13194139541481 17592186576411 true] [17592186058961 1080 "$$3.19$ per gallon" 13194139541481 17592186576411 false] [17592186058961 1080 "$\\$3.19$ per gallon" 13194139541481 17592186576411 true] [17592186059595 1074 "The continuously compounded growth equation is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} P &= P_0e^{rt}. \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe have a final amount of $P=20\\,500$, a rate of $r=0.052$, and a time duration of $t=14$ days. Substituting these values into the formula and solving for $P_0$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nP &= P_{0}e^{rt} \\\\\n20500 &= P_{0}e^{(0.052)(14)} \\\\\n20500 &= P_{0}e^{0.728} \\\\\n20500 &= P_{0}(2.07093...) \\\\\nP_{0} &= \\frac{20500}{2.07093...} \\\\\n&= P_{0} \\mid \\approx 9899\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, there were $9\\,899$ bacteria initially." 13194139541481 17592186576411 false] [17592186059595 1074 "The continuously compounded growth equation is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} P &= P_0e^{rt}. \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe have a final amount of $P=20\\,500$, a rate of $r=0.052$, and a time duration of $t=14$ days. Substituting these values into the formula and solving for $P_0$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nP &= P_{0}e^{rt} \\\\\n20500 &= P_{0}e^{(0.052)(14)} \\\\\n20500 &= P_{0}e^{0.728} \\\\\n20500 &= P_{0}(2.07093...) \\\\\nP_{0} &= \\frac{20500}{2.07093...} \\\\\nP_{0} &\\approx 9899\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, there were $9\\,899$ bacteria initially." 13194139541481 17592186576411 true] [17592186060056 1074 "The continuously compounded growth equation is $P=P_0e^{rt}$. Here $P_0=102$, $P=10$, and $r=-0.095$ per year. Solve for $t$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n10 &= 102e^{-0.095t} \\\\\ne^{-0.095t} &= \\frac{10}{102} \\\\\n-0.095t &= \\ln\\left(\\frac{10}{102}\\right) \\\\\nt &= \\frac{\\ln(10/102)}{-0.095} \\\\\n&\\approx 24.4462.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nRounding to the nearest integer gives $24$ years." 13194139541481 17592186576411 true] [17592186060057 1074 "The continuously compounded growth equation is $P=P_0e^{rt}$. Here $P_0=10$, $P=781$, and $t=14$ minutes. Solve for $r$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n781 &= 10e^{14r} \\\\\ne^{14r} &= \\frac{781}{10} \\\\\n14r &= \\ln\\left(\\frac{781}{10}\\right) \\\\\nr &= \\frac{\\ln(781/10)}{14} \\\\\n&\\approx 0.311285.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe percentage rate is approximately $31.1285\\%$ per minute. Rounding to the nearest percent gives $31\\%$ per minute." 13194139541481 17592186576411 true] [17592186060058 1074 "The continuously compounded growth equation is $P=P_0e^{rt}$. Here $P_0=4120$, $r=-0.0381$ per year, and $t=2016-2009=7$ years. Substitute:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nP &= 4120e^{(-0.0381)(7)} \\\\\n&= 4120e^{-0.2667} \\\\\n&\\approx 3155.5196.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nRounding to the nearest integer gives approximately $3156$ crimes in $2016$." 13194139541481 17592186576411 true] [17592186060059 1074 "The continuously compounded growth equation is $P=P_0e^{rt}$. Here $P_0=9830$ and $r=-0.18$ per day. Convert $2$ weeks to $t=14$ days, then substitute:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nP &= 9830e^{(-0.18)(14)} \\\\\n&= 9830e^{-2.52} \\\\\n&\\approx 790.9179.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nRounding to the nearest integer gives approximately $791$ people." 13194139541481 17592186576411 true] [17592186060238 1074 "The continuously compounded growth equation is $P=P_0e^{rt}$. Here $P=16700$, $r=0.15$ per year, and $t=5$ years. Solve for the earlier profit $P_0$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n16700 &= P_0e^{(0.15)(5)} \\\\\nP_0 &= \\frac{16700}{e^{0.75}} \\\\\n&\\approx 7888.5214.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nRounding to the nearest dollar, the profit five years ago was $\\$7889$." 13194139541481 17592186576411 true] [17592186060389 1074 "The continuously compounded growth equation is $P=P_0e^{rt}$. Here $P=3.11$, $r=-0.01$ per month, and $t=5$ months. Solve for the earlier gas price $P_0$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n3.11 &= P_0e^{(-0.01)(5)} \\\\\nP_0 &= \\frac{3.11}{e^{-0.05}} \\\\\n&\\approx 3.269453.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nRounding to the nearest cent, the earlier price was $\\$3.27$ per gallon." 13194139541481 17592186576411 true]] :edb/tempids {}}
